# This tool's output. It carries your SteamID64, profile URL, country and complete
# library with playtimes. If you clone this repo and run the script inside it, these
# rules are what stand between that and an accidental `git add -A`.
steam_library.csv
steam_library_report.md
steam_library_raw.json

# The same data under any other name. People rename exports, date them, and keep
# copies, and the rules above only match three exact filenames.
steam_library*.csv
steam_library*.md
steam_library*.json

# Anywhere the API key might get parked. The script reads $STEAM_API_KEY, and the
# obvious way to make that persist is a file right here.
.env
.env.*
*.key
steam_key*
*_secret*
*token*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
